thor":"I Aldridge","year":"2013","journal-title":"High-Frequency Trading: A Practical Guide to Algorithmic Strategies and Trading Systems"},{"issue":"2","key":"ref4","first-page":"134","article-title":"Decentralized Oracles: Security and Trust in the Blockchain Ecosystem","volume":"5","author":"B Cornell","year":"2018","journal-title":"Journal of Blockchain Research"},{"issue":"3","key":"ref5","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"967","DOI":"10.1111\/jofi.12498","article-title":"The Flash Crash: The Impact of High Frequency Trading on an Electronic Market","volume":"72","author":"A Kirilenko","year":"2017","journal-title":"The Journal of Finance"},{"issue":"1","key":"ref6","first-page":"55","article-title":"Evaluating Oracle Performance in DeFi: A Comparative Study","volume":"10","author":"H Li","year":"2022","journal-title":"Blockchain Economics"},{"issue":"4","key":"ref7","first-page":"245","article-title":"Market Data Feeds in Decentralized Finance: Challenges and Opportunities","volume":"8","author":"J Smith","year":"2021","journal-title":"International Journal of Financial Innovation"},{"issue":"1","key":"ref8","first-page":"12","article-title":"Trustless Data Aggregation in Decentralized Oracles","volume":"1","author":"S Zhang","year":"2020","journal-title":"IEEE Transactions on Blockchain"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2025,2,18]],"date-time":"2025-02-18T17:12:08Z","timestamp":1739898728000},"score":29.484303,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/www.ssrn.com\/abstract=5143145"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"references-count":8,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.2139\/ssrn.5143145","published":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"subtype":"preprint"},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,20]],"date-time":"2026-10-20T20:09:11Z","timestamp":1792526951028,"version":"4.5.0"},"reference-count":56,"publisher":"Frontiers Media SA","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2025,1,13]],"date-time":"2025-01-13T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1736726400000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/"}],"content-domain":{"domain":["frontiersin.org"],"crossmark-restriction":true},"short-container-title":["Front. Blockchain"],"abstract":"<jats:p>Agricultural insurance is one of the formal and reliable risk management instruments to cope with agrarian risks. Presently, agricultural insurance products rely heavily on centralized systems that lack transparency and traceability, leading to suboptimal risk assessment and delays in payouts. To address these concerns the fintech industry has started to embrace a popular decentralized technology called blockchain. However, blockchain operates as a deterministic and synchronized state system, which means it cannot directly access real-world data for decentralized applications. A mechanism called oracle is required for the trusted access of agricultural risk factor data to smart contracts from external sources such as Internet of Things (IoT) devices, web services and databases. Hence, the present study proposes a blockchain-based AgriInsureDON framework with a privacy-preserving decentralized oracle for risk factor data access from trusted IoT devices for agricultural insurance. Initially, a method for computing the direct reputation score of IoT devices based on behavioral and data reputation is illustrated. Next, a privacy preserved decentralized oracle mechanism is designed and implemented using a masked secret sharing and secure aggregation scheme. Later, we demonstrate the working of weather-indexed insurance contracts based on decentralized oracle. Finally, a performance analysis of smart contract transactions w.r.t average latency, throughput, average CPU utilization and total memory usage is conducted on Ganache and Sepolia test networks. The evaluation results of privacy-protected decentralized oracle and an indexed insurance contract within AgriInsureDON framework confirms that transactions are efficient and scalable to meet the requirements of expedited claim settlement.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.3389\/fbloc.2024.1481339","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2025,1,13]],"date-time":"2025-01-13T11:24:06Z","timestamp":1736767446000},"update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.3389\/crossmark-policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":14,"title":["Blockchain oracles for decentralized agricultural insurance using trusted IoT data"],"prefix":"10.3389","volume":"7","author":[{"given":"Manoj","family":"T","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Krishnamoorthi","family":"Makkithaya","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Narendra","family":"V. G.","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Vijaya Murari","family":"T","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"1965","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2025,1,13]]},"reference":[{"key":"B1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"42","DOI":"10.1186\/s13677-023-00416-8","article-title":"Iot trust and reputation: a survey and taxonomy","volume":"12","author":"Aaqib","year":"2023","journal-title":"J. Cloud Comput."},{"key":"B2","article-title":"Report of the task force on enhancing technology use in agriculture insurance","author":"Aggarwal","year":"2016"},{"key":"B3","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"85675","DOI":"10.1109\/ACCESS.2020.2992698","article-title":"Trustworthy blockchain oracles: review, comparison, and open research challenges","volume":"8","author":"Al-Breiki","year":"2020","journal-title":"IEEE Access"},{"key":"B4","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"445","DOI":"10.14569\/IJACSA.2021.0120153","article-title":"Blockchain in insurance: exploratory analysis of prospects and threats","volume":"12","author":"Amponsah","year":"2021","journal-title":"Int. J. Adv. Comput. Sci. Appl."},{"key":